or a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:49:53-08:00","id":1289948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1268346-unorthodox-settings-eras?p=1289922#post1289922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't recall where, but somewhere in one of the books (either origin or hero) they mention a Scion League of Baseball.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baseball is probably the only sport (at least of the most popular) that a regular professional would be in the same league as Scions... \ud83d\udc8a\ud83d\udc89","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T20:15:45-08:00","id":1290644,"title":"","content":"I could see a Sci-Fi setting taking the form of a galactic &quot;land grab&quot; campaign between the various pantheons and their followers. Maybe have it set in a time period where the earth is no longer capable of sustaining life the same way it used to, and the survivors decide to colonize the stars in search of new worlds on which to thrive.<br /> <br /> This, of course, gives each of the pantheons a golden opportunity to establish themselves as the dominant power of several new worlds, and they send their Scions out into the galaxy to erect their colonies and establish first contact with the indigenous life forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T22:33:57-08:00","id":1290656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caelene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1268346-unorthodox-settings-eras?p=1289744#post1289744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite sure that it counts, but I've had the idea of running something of an 'open' setting ala Aberrant where the existence of the demigods was known to the public. Still working on the details, though. &gt;.&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>... You mean like, the Default 2e setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T23:57:02-08:00","id":1290668,"title":"","content":"I didn\u2019t think Hel was listed anywhere as having a specific fate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1268346-unorthodox-settings-eras?p=1289384#post1289384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bMy understanding is that those who die are:<ul><li>Odin (killed by Fenrir)</li> <li>Freyr (killed by Surtr)</li> <li>Thor (killed by Jormungandr)</li> <li>Tyr (killed by Garm)</li> <li>Heimdall (killed by Loki)</li> <li>Loki (killed by Heimdall)</li> <li>Bragi (killed by some sort of dwarven boar; I'm not clear on the full story)</li> <li>Ve (Odin's brother, also killed by Fenrir or killed by an elf by mistake)</li> <li>Hel</li> <li>Meili</li> <li>Njord (doesn't actually fight; killed when Surtr destroys Vanaheim)</li> <li>Snotra</li> <li>Nanna (Baldar's wife, dies before Ragnarok of a broken heart after Baldar's murder)</li> <li>Gna</li> </ul><br /> The survivors are:<ul><li>AEgir (sea jotun allied with Asgard)</li> <li>Vidar</li> <li>Vali</li> <li>Hoenir</li> <li>Modi</li> <li>Magni</li> <li>Hermodr</li> <li>Forseti</li> <li>Ullr</li> <li>Firgg</li> <li>Freya</li> <li>Sif</li> <li>Thrud</li> <li>Idun</li> <li>Saga</li> <li>Eir</li> <li>Gefjun</li> <li>Fulla</li> <li>Sjofn</li> <li>Lofn</li> <li>Var</li> <li>Vor</li> <li>Syn</li> <li>Hiln</li> </ul>In addition, Baldar and Hodr return from the dead to co-rule over the survivors. <br /> <br /> That's my rough grasp of it, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T00:21:16-08:00","id":1290674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thrythlind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1268346-unorthodox-settings-eras?p=1290668#post1290668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn\u2019t think Hel was listed anywhere as having a specific fate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not certain. At least one thing I remember reading years ago was the presumption that the reason Baldar was able to return was Hel having died, but I have no idea what it might've been based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:15:46-08:00","id":1292348,"title":"","content":"Mythic Eras: Bogatyri (The Russian/Eastern Slavic pantheon in the Kievan Rus in 980 to 1015AD) - introducing the Russian pantheon (the Bogovi?) if they aren't already presented somewhere.<br /> <br /> Mythic Eras: The Golden Horde (the Mongolia/Tengrist pantheon during the period of the Mongolian Empire in the 13th century) - again introducing the Tengrist pantheon if not already presented.<br /> <br /> Mythic Eras: Zululand (the Zulu pantheon in the Zulu Kingdom during the reign of Shaka, 1818 - 1828) - introducing the Zulu pantheon.<br /> <br /> Added: Mythic Eras: Black Warriors (the Muskogee pantheon in the Southeastern US in about 1540) - introducing the Muskogee pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-27-2019, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T21:49:29-08:00","id":1295210,"title":"","content":"An odd one that occurred to me: Many years ago, Richard Garfinkle wrote a book called Celestial Matters, set in a world where Alexander the Great's empire lasted far longer and was much bigger. And also, Classical Greek science and cosmology are true. Because the plot of the novel is an expedition to the sun to retrieve a piece of it to use as a super weapon against the Chinese Empire. It is a really fun book that I recommend if you can find a copy. But I also think it could make for a really interesting Scion setting. I'm not really sure what the divine situation would be like, as I can't recall any specifics on the subject from the book, but I suspect it would involve some odd mingling after 900 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T11:29:45-07:00","id":1297542,"title":"","content":"Has anyone tried straight out fantasy settings? Either single or multiple pantheons? I ask because I had the idea of an Egyptian based one - likely with a Mediterranean and Nile River Basin based Geography/Climate - where the Atenism heresy succeeds in supplanting the Netjer and, several hundred years later, has morphed into this fairly oppressive and tyrannical theocratic dictatorship, complete with Inquisition secret police. And into this, the old gods decide it is time for a new generation of Heroes to arise and return the world to proper Ma'at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}